# IR Fixtures

Generated from ../src/*.c, *.cu and *.hip by scripts/regenerate_fixtures.sh
with clang 15:

  *.ll, *.opt.yaml  clang --target=arm64-apple-macos13 -mcpu=apple-m1 -O2
                    -gline-tables-only -fno-discard-value-names
                    -fsave-optimization-record -S -emit-llvm
  x86/*.ll          the same for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu (different
                    unrolling; math-errno on by default)
  nodebug/*.ll      arm64 without debug info (and without the optimization
                    record, which would make clang keep locations)
  gpu_*.ll          CUDA device code: -x cuda --cuda-device-only
                    --cuda-gpu-arch=sm_70 -nocudainc -nocudalib (no SDK
                    needed; ../src/cuda_shim.h stands in for its headers)
  hip_*.ll          HIP device code: -x hip --cuda-device-only
                    --offload-arch=gfx90a -nogpuinc -nogpulib
  unoptimized.ll    reduction.c at -O0; the analyzer must refuse it
  ident_mismatch.ll saxpy.ll claiming clang 17; the analyzer must warn

The targets are pinned so results (vector widths, cost decisions, gather
support) don't depend on the machine running the tests. Each source file
documents the problem it contains; test/CMakeLists.txt asserts the expected
findings and rejects known false positives.

Regenerate after changing a source or upgrading clang, then re-run ctest.
